@model GuidePageViewModel
@* QE@@Home: how-it-works section. Edit content here; layout, navigation and footer are in Views/Shared/_QEatHomeLayout.cshtml. *@
  <div class="hero"><div class="hero-img" style="background-image:url(/qe-at-home/img/classroom17.jpg);background-position:55% 70%"></div>
    <div class="in"><div class="kicker">Section 2</div><h1>How Distance Learning Works</h1></div>
  </div>
  <section class="block">
    <div class="wrap grid2">
      <div>
        <h2>Our Approach</h2>
        <p>Every phase uses a balanced blend of three kinds of learning, adjusted to the age of the children:</p>
        <ul class="tick">
          <li><strong>Live sessions</strong> with teachers and classmates, at set times in the day, for direct teaching, questioning and discussion.</li>
          <li><strong>Structured independent tasks</strong> that consolidate what has been taught live, or prepare for the next session.</li>
          <li><strong>Offline activities</strong> that give children time away from the screen.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We ensure equitable access through printed materials or device support where needed, and use flexible assessment, such as formative checks and project-based tasks, so that teachers can see how each child is getting on and give regular feedback.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2>The Learning Day</h2>
        <p>We aim to make provision in line with current Ministry of Education guidance. Daily learning time includes live sessions, follow-up tasks and offline activities, not time in front of a screen.</p>
        <div class="tbl"><table>
          <tr><th>Phase</th><th>Daily learning time</th><th>Live sessions</th></tr>
          <tr><td class="k">Pre-Prep</td><td>About 2.5 hours</td><td>3 to 5 short sessions a day, up to 15 minutes each</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="k">Prep</td><td>About 3 to 3.5 hours</td><td>3 to 4 a day (Year 1) or 4 a day (Years 2 to 6), 15 to 20 minutes each</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="k">Senior School</td><td>About 4.5 hours</td><td>The normal timetable, each lesson finishing five minutes early</td></tr>
        </table></div>
        <p class="note">All times on this site are UAE time.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="block alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Platforms at a Glance</h2>
      <p>Each phase uses the platforms your child already knows. Microsoft Teams is our approved platform for live lessons across the school.</p>
      <div class="tbl"><table>
        <tr><th>Phase</th><th>Live lessons</th><th>Work and resources</th><th>Updates for families</th></tr>
        <tr><td class="k">Pre-Prep</td><td>Microsoft Teams; the link is shared ahead of time and stays the same for each teacher</td><td>Seesaw, using your child’s own student login</td><td>Email for formal communication; Seesaw for the day ahead, including session links</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="k">Prep</td><td>Microsoft Teams, with breakout rooms used to adapt learning</td><td>Seesaw, plus the distance learning pack, The Good Morning Club, Times Tables Rock Stars and Spelling Shed</td><td>Email for formal communication; Seesaw for the day ahead</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="k">Senior School</td><td>Microsoft Teams, from the Teams calendar or the Class Team</td><td>Teams: meeting chat, class channels, the Shared tab and Teams Assignments</td><td>Teams year group updates and email</td></tr>
      </table></div>
      <div class="grid3" style="margin-top:28px">
        <div class="card"><h3>Devices</h3><p>Every student has a school-managed device. Where a family does not have the technology needed, the school will consider lending a device where circumstances permit. Please talk to us early.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Technical support</h3><p>Our IT team, under the Director of Operations, will issue protocols for getting help. If a problem stops your child joining, tell their class teacher or tutor so work can be shared another way.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Weekly updates</h3><p>The Principal will send a weekly update to the whole community throughout any period of distance learning.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
